# ---> Go
# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# The built binary (module name, produced by `go build`/`go build ./...`
# in the repo root)
/tangsible

# Per-directory invocation-history state `run`/`rerun`/`role` auto-write to
# the cwd (see CLAUDE.md's Rerun section) - local run history, not project
# source, and can carry hostnames/tags/extra-vars from past invocations.
# .tangsible/config.toml is deliberately NOT ignored here - unlike
# state.toml, it's user-authored settings (design-docs/
# Dottangsible-directory.md), never written by Tangsible itself, and safe
# (often desirable) to commit and share across a team.
/.tangsible/state.toml

# Per-generation saved run data (design-docs/Revisit.md) - each
# ansible-playbook generation's raw jsonl stdout and collected stderr,
# referenced by RunID from state.toml above. Same reasoning as
# state.toml itself: local, app-written, and can carry real command
# output/hostnames.
/.tangsible/runs/

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.claude/

